  (
    'berkshire-hathaway-brk-b-the-safest-cheap-stock-on-wall-street-or-a-very',
    'Berkshire Hathaway ($BRK.B): The Safest “Cheap” Stock on Wall Street, or a Very Expensive Hedge?',
    'Berkshire Hathaway does not trend on FinTwit. It does not ride AI hype cycles. And it certainly does not promise to 10x your money. Yet in a market obsessed with growth at any price, Berkshire is quietly being called one of the cheapest safe stocks you can buy today. Massive cash pile. Fortress…',
    '{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Berkshire Hathaway does not trend on FinTwit. It does not ride AI hype cycles. And it certainly does not promise to 10x your money."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yet in a market obsessed with growth at any price, Berkshire is quietly being called one of the cheapest safe stocks you can buy today. Massive cash pile. Fortress balance sheet. Legendary capital allocation. No hype."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"At first glance, the case feels almost too clean."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"But scratch beneath the surface, and Berkshire’s appeal becomes far more subtle and far more debatable than the headlines suggest."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"So is Berkshire truly undervalued, or is it simply priced exactly where it should be?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Let’s unpack it.","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"horizontalRule"},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"🧮 The “Hidden Valuation” Argument"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The bullish case often starts with this claim:"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"“Berkshire looks expensive on the surface, but strip out the cash and investments, and the operating businesses are cheap.”"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"There is truth here, with caveats."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Berkshire holds an enormous cash position north of $350B and a massive marketable securities portfolio. If you subtract those assets and focus only on the operating businesses, the implied multiple falls meaningfully below that of comparable industrial companies."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"On paper, that makes Berkshire look like a bargain."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"But here is the catch. You cannot subtract the cash from the valuation without also subtracting the earnings that cash generates. Doing so double counts value."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Once you correctly remove interest income from earnings, Berkshire’s operating multiple rises closer to the mid teens. It is not absurdly cheap, but it is not stretched either."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"In other words, the 10 to 12 times earnings narrative is overly optimistic. The reality is closer to 15 to 16 times, depending on assumptions."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Still reasonable. Just not magic."}]},{"type":"horizontalRule"},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"🏦 The Ultimate Capital Allocation Vehicle"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Where Berkshire genuinely stands apart is not valuation. It is optionality."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Berkshire is not just a company. It is an actively managed capital allocation machine operating inside a publicly traded wrapper."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You are not just buying businesses like GEICO, BNSF, or Berkshire Hathaway Energy. You are outsourcing some of the hardest decisions in investing:"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"When to deploy cash"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"Where to deploy it"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"How aggressively to act in a crisis"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Historically, Berkshire has been offered deals retail investors will never see. Preferred shares, structured financings, and rescue capital on terms that only emerge during panic."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"That is the appeal."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Not that Berkshire will outperform every year, but that when markets break, Berkshire tends to have a seat at the table."}]},{"type":"horizontalRule"},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"🛡️ The “Free Put”, or a Drag on Returns?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Supporters describe Berkshire’s cash pile as a free put option on the market."}]},{"type":"image","attrs":{"src":"/imported/berkshire-hathaway-brk-b-the-safest-cheap-stock-on-wall-street-or-a-very/2.webp","alt":"","caption":""}},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"If markets crash, Berkshire has dry powder."},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"If nothing happens, cash earns interest and preserves flexibility."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"But critics push back hard."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Holding cash is not free."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Cash drags returns in bull markets."},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"Cash is exposed to currency debasement."},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"Cash requires exceptional timing to justify its opportunity cost."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"And here is the uncomfortable truth. Berkshire sat on cash during one of the strongest bull runs in modern history."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"That discipline protects downside, but it also caps upside."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Which raises the key question."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Are you buying Berkshire to grow faster than the market, or to survive when the market does not?"}]},{"type":"horizontalRule"},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"⚙️ The Operating Reality Beneath the Brand"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Another overlooked nuance is that many of Berkshire’s crown jewels are capital intensive businesses."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Railroads require constant reinvestment just to maintain earnings."},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"Utilities must pour capital into infrastructure to stay competitive."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"That means reported operating earnings can overstate true owner earnings."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"In valuation terms, these businesses deserve lower multiples, not higher ones. That narrows the margin of safety further."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Berkshire is resilient."},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"It is not structurally high growth."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Scale is both its advantage and its ceiling."}]},{"type":"horizontalRule"},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"🧠 Buffett, Abel, and the “Post Legend” Discount"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The market often frames leadership transition as a risk."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"In Berkshire’s case, it may already be priced in."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Greg Abel has effectively been running large portions of the business for years. The system is institutionalised. Capital allocation decisions are no longer a one man show."}]},{"type":"image","attrs":{"src":"/imported/berkshire-hathaway-brk-b-the-safest-cheap-stock-on-wall-street-or-a-very/3.webp","alt":"","caption":""}},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Ironically, the so called Buffett premium may already be gone."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"What remains is the machine."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The open question is not whether Berkshire survives Buffett. It is whether future capital allocation can meaningfully move the needle at this scale."}]},{"type":"horizontalRule"},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"📉 Cheap, Compared to What?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This is where the debate really lands."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Compared to mega cap tech priced for perfection, speculative AI narratives with thin margins, and levered growth stories dependent on cheap capital, Berkshire looks conservative, rational, and almost boring."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"But compared to risk free rates near 4 percent, a narrow equity risk premium, and historical Berkshire valuation multiples, it looks closer to fair value than deep value."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"That does not make it a bad investment."},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"It just reframes expectations."}]},{"type":"horizontalRule"},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"🔚 Bottom Line"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Berkshire Hathaway is not a meme stock."},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"It is not a growth rocket."},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"And it is probably not cheap in the classic sense."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"What it is:"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A hedge against chaos"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"A bet on disciplined capital allocation"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"A way to outsource decision making in moments when most investors panic"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Whether that is worth today’s price depends less on spreadsheets and more on how you think the next decade unfolds."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"If markets stay calm and compounding dominates, Berkshire may lag."},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"If volatility returns and capital discipline matters again, Berkshire’s patience may finally be rewarded."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Sometimes the most interesting investments are not about upside."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"They are about who you trust to be holding the cash when everyone else is forced to sell.","marks":[{"type":"bold"},{"type":"italic"}]}]}]}'::jsonb,
    '/imported/berkshire-hathaway-brk-b-the-safest-cheap-stock-on-wall-street-or-a-very/1.webp',
