  (
    'asx-small-cap-gems-uos',
    'ASX Small Cap Gems – UOS',
    'Over the past year – many of Australia’s ASX listed large caps have seen typical inclinations within its stock price, from Commonwealths Banks +46.00% (in the past year) to Telstra Group Limited which saw an increase of +35.46%. Although large caps such as CSL Limited and BHP Group said otherwise…',
    '{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Over the past year – many of Australia’s ASX listed large caps have seen typical inclinations within its stock price, from Commonwealths Banks +46.00% (in the past year) to Telstra Group Limited which saw an increase of +35.46%. Although large caps such as CSL Limited and BHP Group said otherwise within the top 9 largest caps listed, with plunges of 14.31% and 17.52% respectively."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, these large caps do seem very enticing to buy most of the time, but it’s safe to say there are some hidden small caps in sight that are gems. Just like a diamond in the rough."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A quick glance of small-caps such as Multistack International Limited and Key Petroleum Limited, show negative market-cap performance followed by a subsequent negative diluted EPS. Two indicative figures of not only increasing volatility but profitability during tumultuous downfalls. Just to mention, Key Petroleum had a fall of 99.58% in the last financial year, highlighting such extremities."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"As we mentioned, there are some companies out there that paint a different picture, without a further ado, let’s get into one of them."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"UOS- United Overseas Australia Limited"}]},{"type":"image","attrs":{"src":"/imported/asx-small-cap-gems-uos/1.webp","alt":"","caption":""}},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"United Overseas Australia Pty Ltd is an investment holding company which currently engages in property development, investment, management and construction."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The holding company is called UOA Group and it was founded and listed on the ASX in 1987 and since 1989, it has based its headquarters and business operations in Kuala Lumpur."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"“UOA’s investment strategy is to invest in good investment grade commercial and residential assets in prime, high return growth areas.” – UOA.com","marks":[{"type":"italic"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"As of 31 December 2023, the Group has successfully developed and delivered many projects, this includes in the commercial, retail and the residential realm, with an estimated GDV (Gross Development Value) in excess of an estimated 21.0 Billion RM (7 Billion AUD."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"There’s still over 80 acres that need to be developed and the company has developed an investment portfolio (primarily REITs) in excess of 3.8 Billion RM (1.3 Billion AUD)."}]},{"type":"image","attrs":{"src":"/imported/asx-small-cap-gems-uos/2.webp","alt":"","caption":"“The UOA REIT investment portfolio includes six key UOA commercial properties – namely UOA Centre and UOA II, UOA Damansara, UOA Damansara II, Menara UOA Bangsar and UOA Corporate Tower – valued at approximately RM1.72 billion.” (UOA Group)."}},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"It’s safe to say the size and ability to upscale production to achieve high quality properties with such immense value and traction is a reason why UOS is a market leader and a force within the property development industry."}]},{"type":"horizontalRule"},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Financial Overview"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"As of 3/7/2025, UOSs current market-cap is 1.09B which makes it an ASX listed small-cap, making it the first instance of a very volatile firm. The P/E is 10.81 and the diluted EPS is 0.06AUD, which suggests that investors are very willing to invest relative to each dollar of the company’s earnings, highlighting a major overvaluation. The overvaluation can be balanced however, by the slight profit that is evident through the diluted EPS of 0.06 (TTM), which is further encouraging as the value has seen a change of +11.67% within the past 12 months."}]},{"type":"image","attrs":{"src":"/imported/asx-small-cap-gems-uos/3.webp","alt":"","caption":""}},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The relative volume however, is 0.02, indicated by a current volume of 1k, meaning that an average volume is 50k, this discrepancy may highlight the external markets sentiment towards UOS, one that is risky, especially due to its shaky past performance (-16.08% change in stock in the past 5 years although quelled by a +15.38% increase in the past 10)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the current data, it seems we can make a criteria."}]},{"type":"table","content":[{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph"}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Relative Volume"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph"}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"———–"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Market Cap"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph"}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"———–"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"P/E"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"————-"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"EPS Dilution"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"————-"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"EPS Diluted Growth"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"————-"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the table above, at first glance, yes, the upside is favoured slightly, although the price is still volatile, highlighted by the -0.40 Beta (in the past year) which is indicative of the risk associated with such an acquisition. What’s encouraging and balances this statement is the pattern that can be seen throughout the last 5 years, although there has been some short down-turns, there always seems to be some bullish behaviour thereafter, especially when broadening the landscape. The steep upturn seen after a steady fall in stock price can be seen in 3 stages, most recently between 2020 and 2022. But there seems to be some sort of a slow and steady resurgence since that time frame."}]},{"type":"image","attrs":{"src":"/imported/asx-small-cap-gems-uos/4.webp","alt":"","caption":""}},{"type":"horizontalRule"},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":3},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Valuation Analysis"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Note –> PEG on 4/7/2025, 1.00"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"PEG is currently 0.93 which suggests the the price that investors are willing to invest is almost to the expected earnings growth within the future, showing close to a fair valuation. However, the P/S is 2.95. It is worth mentioning that the market-cap is currently 1.03 billion which is currently nearly 2 times the current revenue that had been accumulated. Although this may show an overvaluation by investors, both the market-cap performance and the revenue accumulated for 1Y has both seen decent performance increases, being 0.86% and 23.34% respectively. This is especially encouraging since the volatility has only deviated by 0.19% between the past month and week, highlighting a positive outlook on future valuation."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The P/CF is currently at 18.28, hinting at a severe overvaluation by investors while the P/FCF is even higher at 23.52.This is due to the operating cash flow currently being at 55.18MAUD and the Capital Expenditure currently being at -12.31M. It showcases how investors are paying more for each dollar of cash flow and free-cash flow, although the Price/Cash is 1.26 and the EV Value is 1.42B, highlighting a net balance of positive activity. This is because investors are not being too overboard based on the cash on hand, especially since it has been identified that that the Cash & Equivalents can greatly take care of the debt incurred (803.36M : 279.60M)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The downside that has been consistently seen has been the overvaluations, but we can say that it can be mitigated through positive internal balances, for example the P/FCF can be balanced through the encouraging status of the current EV Value."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"It is also worth mentioning for future investors that YOY, there has been an increase in the revenue accumulated from 2022 to 202, and also the Net Income. Although, the P/E and P/S have both consistently fallen in recent years, for example the P/S has has seen a fall from approximately 3.5 to 2.95, highlighting how there is closer proximity to a reasonable valuation (preferably 1.00) within the near future."}]},{"type":"image","attrs":{"src":"/imported/asx-small-cap-gems-uos/5.webp","alt":"","caption":""}},{"type":"horizontalRule"},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Noteworthy Information","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"It is worth noting that Simply Wall Street mentioned that the industry percentage for other renumeration is lower than that of UOS, which signifies that there is much higher performance, especially within the current real estate market. However, investors would probably prefer not to see that the CEO’s salary is far in excess of the median. However, renumeration and CEO base pay should not really be the main focal point when it comes to an investors buy or sell decision, instead, they should take a much more holistic approach in their decisions."}]},{"type":"image","attrs":{"src":"/imported/asx-small-cap-gems-uos/6.webp","alt":"","caption":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/au/real-estate-management-and-development/asx-uos/united-overseas-australia-shares/news/we-think-some-shareholders-may-hesitate-to-increase-united-o"}},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"On June 4th, TipRanks also reported of the reasoning of the most recent UOS rise in shares. This is due to the influx of 22 million ordinary fully paid securities as part of a dividend or distribution plan, this would allow a greater impact in stakeholder interest due to rise in the number of securities that would circulate within the market. "},{"type":"text","text":"(","marks":[{"type":"italic"}]},{"type":"text","text":"https://www.tipranks.com/news/catalyst/why-united-overseas-australia-ltd-shares-are-rising","marks":[{"type":"italic"},{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"https://www.tipranks.com/news/catalyst/why-united-overseas-australia-ltd-shares-are-rising"}}]},{"type":"text","text":")","marks":[{"type":"italic"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"What remains reassuring that although there may be some hesitation, it is safe to say that UOS does remain a positive sentiment for investors to buy, especially as their position within the real estate and property development sector and landscape continues to change."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Unfortunately, there has not been any more publicly stated updates but its shares and relative activity continues to be very active. It still is, if you remember, a market leader in its own right within the real estate sector."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"That being said, is it an emerald…no….but is it a diamond in the rough, yes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Reference Links:","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Source","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/ASX-UOS/?timeframe=YTD"}}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Source","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"https://uoa.com.my/investor-relations/uoa-ltd/corporate-information/general/"}}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Source","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/au/real-estate-management-and-development/asx-uos/united-overseas-australia-shares/news/we-think-some-shareholders-may-hesitate-to-increase-united-o"}}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Source","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"https://www.tipranks.com/news/catalyst/why-united-overseas-australia-ltd-shares-are-rising"}}]}]},{"type":"horizontalRule"},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Author – Natesh Nagarajah"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"8/7/2025, 7:51pm AEST,Melbourne (Australia)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Linkedin: "},{"type":"text","text":"http://www.linkedin.com/in/natesh-n-94454a277","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"http://www.linkedin.com/in/natesh-n-94454a277"}}]}]}]}'::jsonb,
