  (
    'next-technology-holding-inc-quality-or-not',
    'Next Technology Holding Inc. – Quality or Not?',
    'Founded in 2019, Next Technology Holding Inc, as per the name suggests, resides within the Technology Services sector, which due to the rapid expansion of AI technologies and its alternatives, seems to be one of fastest growing sectors in modern markets, if not the fastest. More specifically, Next…',
    '{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Founded in 2019, Next Technology Holding Inc, as per the name suggests, resides within the Technology Services sector, which due to the rapid expansion of AI technologies and its alternatives, seems to be one of fastest growing sectors in modern markets, if not the fastest. More specifically, Next Technologies is more of what is considered a Packaging Software company, which involves that production, distribution and development of commercially available software programs."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Weihong Liu remains the CEO of the holding company since January 2024 and overseeas the developments that occur within the headquarters located in Shenzen, China. Weighong Liu has a vast array of experience within investments and research, spanning over 6 years. Liu has plans to expand the companies within the tech and AI fields and holds strong executive ability in the corporate construction field. Liu holds a Bachelor’s Degree of Business Management from the Univeristy of West. England."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Not to mention, the company as per Trading View, has 6 employees as reported within the last financial year, generating nearly $300,000 USD ($500,000 AUD) per employee – Revenue/Employee. This hence, generates 3.59M USD ($5 M AUD) for every employee – Net Income/Employee for the last financial year. It’s safe to say on face-value that each employee is contributing adequately for the profit maximization of the firm."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Financial Overview"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"As of 22/6/2025, the NXTT Technologies Holding Inc’s stock pricei is 3.44 USD (+2.11) and an overall increase of +158.65%. The company has a small-cap of 1.50B, highlighting slighting higher volatility due to its size."}]},{"type":"image","attrs":{"src":"/imported/next-technology-holding-inc-quality-or-not/2.webp","alt":"","caption":""}},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"From the year to date, we can easily see the sudden fluctuations in stock price, this has already occurred in 3 phases, firstly in and around mid to late January, where there a relatively higher stock price, followed by a steep decline and a slow reduction from Feb to May. This is followed by a sudden inclination around May 9, then followed by a steep decline (again…) within another rapid increase in June 18. Evidently showing how volatile the companies stock has been in 2025."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"There is currently 75.62M (17.33%) closely held shares and 360.65M (82.67%) free floating shares ready to be acquired. The company is seeing above average volumes of shares being sold (13.83M volume compares to a 13.18 relative volume). The company is seeing a potential overvaluation as the P/E ratio is 1.52, highlighting how the company’s stock is not a reflection of the earnings that they have received from the relevant shares. This is evident through the 2.27 USD EPS dilution which is significantly lower than the current price, even with the inclusion of outstanding shares within the market. Although, it does hint at the fact that Next Technology Holding is still raking in profits, just not at the level the level that investors currently think it is."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Its safe to say as per the figures mentioned, there is a potential overvaluation by investors for a relatively volatile company, but its still making profits."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"We will dig even further later to highlight its true state."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Questionable Valuations"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The company currently has a P/S ratio of 72.12, this may have been because of the increase of the market cap for the company, which is now 1.5B (+4.356.25%) in comparison to its revenue. As there has been a subsequent increase in the P/S, this may suggest that investors are more willing to pay for a share for each subsequent sale carried out by the company. This highlights not only current but future growth."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Next Technology Holding Inc. has a beta of -0.73, emphasising the slight risk and subsequent volatility status. Additionally, the EV value is at 1.02 B, however the company has incurred some level of debt."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The P/CF ratio currently sits at 633,505.40, this looks like a very big number on the face, but it shows that investors are willing to pay depending due to the current cash generating ability. As mentioned earlier, based on the EPS, there is imminent profitability, which may have swayed investor sentiment and provided an outlook for the CF, but there is still an underlying concern because of two things."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"First is the pattern that was seen in Graph 1, after a tremendous peak, there is a subsequent downfall. However, that is 2025, on an annual basis, the revenue exceeded the net income in 2020 and 2021, before falling into disarray in 2022 and climbing back ever since, leading to net income exceeding revenue in 2025."}]},{"type":"image","attrs":{"src":"/imported/next-technology-holding-inc-quality-or-not/3.webp","alt":"","caption":""}},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Essentially, in 2025, it has been very volatile, although encouraging to some regard, however, it has not seen great progress all-time, possibly due to the expansion of the company as it was only developed during 2019. This included the covid-era, which may have derailed the company during 2022."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"My second point is, the P/E and P/S has actually fallen dramatically from 2020-2024, even with a rise in revenue or net income (as there is an evident imbalance), this correlates to the dramatic slump in stock price that was identified. There was probably less confidence of the companies financial performance due to its fluctuations, leading to a fall in investor sentiment over these time periods."}]},{"type":"image","attrs":{"src":"/imported/next-technology-holding-inc-quality-or-not/4.webp","alt":"","caption":""}},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Profitability Outlook"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"As mentioned earlier, there has been an imbalance in the revenue and net income for some years. Most recently in 2024, it has been reported that the net income has outweighed the revenue by a significant margin. Although what is worth mentioning is that in Q4 2024, the companies debt had outweighed the cash & equivalents by nearly 100k USD, not to mention, in the first quarter for financial year 2025, the debt had more than doubled."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The total revenue trailing in the last 12 months is around $1.8M USD which is a -31.64% revenue decrease, while also the EPS Diluted Growth had fallen by a whopping 74.74%."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"What we can see from these metrics is that there has been quite a fluctuation based on revenue, net income and debts alone, which highlights the instability that the company is currently facing in order to earn profit on a much broader scale, especially as it is seen how the non-operating income/expenses has greatly outweighed the net income."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"But the Question Begs… Is it a Quality Investment or not?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"To simply put it…in my perspective… No."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"As seen, there has been an overvaluation by investors although there has been good signs of profit."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"However, a small-cap firm such as Next Technology Inc. shows signs of volatility through past performance throughout 2020 and 2021, where there was massive peaks that were seen, followed by immense drops in value."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"We can still expect to see this type of behavior, considering the level of beta is at a negative and how the company is facing growing debts by the quarter, although, the company is seeing the highest net income since 2024."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"There are some really good signs, but so much unpredictability."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"UPDATE: 24/06/2025","marks":[{"type":"bold"},{"type":"italic"}]}]},{"type":"image","attrs":{"src":"/imported/next-technology-holding-inc-quality-or-not/5.webp","alt":"","caption":""}},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Next Technology Holding Inc.’s stock has fallen by 37.79%, as predicted, there was a steep decline, with numerous signs of unpredictability and patterns which has hence caused the inevitable."}]},{"type":"image","attrs":{"src":"/imported/next-technology-holding-inc-quality-or-not/6.webp","alt":"","caption":""}},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This is a 6 month outlook showcasing the consistent pattern with the most recent peak on the far right."}]}]}'::jsonb,
    '/imported/next-technology-holding-inc-quality-or-not/1.webp',
    'Next Technology Holding Inc. – Quality or Not?',
