  (
    'weekly-market-inspection-3-pathward-financial-inc',
    'Weekly Market Inspection #3 – Pathward Financial Inc',
    'Background: Pathward Financial, Inc. mainly conducts itself as a holding company, specializing in savings and loans. The firm also operates within a multitude of sectors, such as Consumer, Commercial, and Corporate Services. The consumer sector includes meta payment systems (MPS), consumer credit…',
    '{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Background:"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Pathward Financial, Inc. mainly conducts itself as a holding company, specializing in savings and loans. The firm also operates within a multitude of sectors, such as Consumer, Commercial, and Corporate Services."}]},{"type":"image","attrs":{"src":"/imported/weekly-market-inspection-3-pathward-financial-inc/1.webp","alt":"","caption":""}},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The consumer sector includes meta payment systems (MPS), consumer credit products, warehouse finance and other tax services. The commercial sector includes the Crestmark and AFS divisions. Moreover, the Corporate Services sector includes insight into shares services, treasury, retained community bank portfolios and student loan lending portfolios."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The company was founded on June 14, 1993 and its headquarters is in Sioux Falls. The current CEO is Brett L. Pharr."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Brett Phar was previously the Co-President and the Chief Operating Officer since June 2020 and also the Executive Vice President, Group Head of Governance, Risk and Compliance since February 2019."}]},{"type":"image","attrs":{"src":"/imported/weekly-market-inspection-3-pathward-financial-inc/2.webp","alt":"","caption":""}},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Before joining Pathward, he also served as the Senior Risk Director at Citizens Bank in the Consumer Division. He had also worked at Bank of America for 32 years, in that time, he was tasked with multiple responsibilities in tandem with his designated roles- some of which included Commercial and consumer lines of business, Business Transformation, Mergers and Acquisitions and Risk, prior to his time in Citizens Bank."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Financial Overview:"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"In terms of Growth and Profitability, comparing the companies recent performance and margins, there has been a gradual increase in the total revenues from 513.36M in 2020, 556M in 2022 and finally 775.94M in 2024. Consequentially, this has allowed an increase in the Net Income, from 104.72M in 2020 to 166.81M in 2024, contributing to a fall in net-margin during this time period. This may have been because although there was an increase in total revenue from 2023 to 2024, expenses may have increased by a greater proportion."}]},{"type":"image","attrs":{"src":"/imported/weekly-market-inspection-3-pathward-financial-inc/3.webp","alt":"","caption":""}},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"In 2024, most of the company’s revenue stream was divided into three main categories, the Consumer, Commercial and the Corporate Services/Other sector. The Consumer sector generate the most revenue, which includes 453.12M USD (60.04%), followed by the Commercial Sector – 266.71M USD (35.34%) and finally the Corporate Services/Other sector which totaled to 34.87M USD (4.62%). As seen, there is a heavy reliance on the Consumer sector to drive company profits."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"It is estimated by October 22nd 2025, the company is forecasted to earn 794.32M USD in revenues and earnings are estimated to value to 7.51 USD."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"During 2020-24, there was also a gradual increase in Net Loans and Total Deposits – HOW DOES THIS IMPACT THE FINANCIAL POSITION?"}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Current State – 10/5/2025"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"As of the 10th of May 2025, Pathward Financials current price is 82.25 USD which is a -0.57% change in stock price. The company is seeing a short-term downside as it’s volume has decreased as its relative volume is 0.48, originating from a 103.94k volume in comparison to its 216.54k average volume."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"However, the company is does have a 1.96B market cap which is pressing the realms of a mid-cap, which could suggest that there is growing levels of relative stability and not too much wavering volatility, especially since the financial services sector is one of the best performing with the US Market. Pathward Financial also has a P/E Ratio of 11.11, underlining the level of overvaluation by investors, who still see positive future growth despite current downturns. This is backed by a 7.40 diluted EPS which suggests that the company is still making a profit which further enhances investor confidence and optimism. In fact, there has been a 11.10% change in diluted EPS in the last 12 months."}]},{"type":"image","attrs":{"src":"/imported/weekly-market-inspection-3-pathward-financial-inc/4.webp","alt":"","caption":"5-year stock movement for Pathward Financial"}},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"As seen within the last 5 years, in May 2020, there was a stock price of 15.60, there has since been a 402.14%, starting with an increase in investor participation during 2021 post-covid, which subsequently the stock price slow-down for the company (reasons will be discussed later) before a gradual increase through to 2025. One thing to mention that there has been an increase in market-cap expansion of 48.83% which has also contributed to the sentiment and overall exchange percentages, fostering a positive inclination in the company’s gradual stock movement."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"So what we are saying is essentially, there is currently a short term downturn but an incentive to buy due to future growth projections."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Valuation Analysis:"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"As mentioned earlier, there was a 48.83% increase in Market Cap performance within the last year and there a subsequent PEG of 1.01, underlining positive economic growth projections. Essentially highlighting how the stock price is moving steadily in conjunction with its future economic growth without any over and under valuation."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The P/S is currently at 2.52 which may have risen due to the increase in market-cap performance by 43.37% (as of 12/5/2025), which significantly outweighed the growth in revenue which according to Tradeview is +3.25%. The current EV Value is 1.74 B USD which in conjunction with an EV/Revenue ratio of 2.23 (TTM) highlights how there is a potential overvaluation of the company as the total value of the company outweighs the revenue earned."}]},{"type":"image","attrs":{"src":"/imported/weekly-market-inspection-3-pathward-financial-inc/5.webp","alt":"","caption":""}},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Overview:"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Short-term downturn but future economic growth potential"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Steady upward trajectory of stock price"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Potential company over-valuation"}]}]}]}]}'::jsonb,
    '/imported/weekly-market-inspection-3-pathward-financial-inc/1.webp',
