  (
    'meta-in-2030-from-ads-to-ai-infrastructure-powerhouse',
    'Meta in 2030: From Ads to AI Infrastructure Powerhouse',
    'Why Meta’s future looks very different from its past Meta’s Transformation Is Already Underway Most people still think of Meta as just a social media company. But under the surface, it’s rapidly evolving into something much bigger. Over the past couple of years, Meta has been quietly but…',
    '{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Why Meta’s future looks very different from its past","marks":[{"type":"italic"}]}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Meta’s Transformation Is Already Underway"}]},{"type":"image","attrs":{"src":"/imported/meta-in-2030-from-ads-to-ai-infrastructure-powerhouse/1.webp","alt":"","caption":""}},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Most people still think of Meta as just a social media company. But under the surface, it’s rapidly evolving into something much bigger. Over the past couple of years, Meta has been quietly but aggressively reshaping its internal structure—cutting costs, shifting priorities, and pouring resources into building a massive AI infrastructure backbone."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"From Social Growth Engine to AI Power Platform"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Between 2012 and 2020, Meta mastered mobile monetisation through Facebook, Instagram, and WhatsApp. But privacy changes and rising regulation slowed the ad machine. Instead of seeing this as the end, Meta used it as a springboard—downsizing projects and doubling down on its technical strengths. Even the widely mocked metaverse push showed that Meta’s leadership isn’t afraid to bet big on the future."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"That mindset is now fuelling its pivot to AI tools, platforms, and internal systems—with visible results."}]},{"type":"image","attrs":{"src":"/imported/meta-in-2030-from-ads-to-ai-infrastructure-powerhouse/2.webp","alt":"","caption":""}},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Financial Muscle Behind the Shift"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Meta is still a financial juggernaut. In Q1 2025, it pulled in $42.3 billion in revenue, with a net margin over 32%. And it’s investing aggressively: up to $72 billion in capital spending this year, mostly on AI infrastructure. This isn’t wasteful spending—it’s core to building scalable, cost-efficient AI systems."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yet, Meta is still rewarding shareholders—returning nearly $70 billion via buybacks and dividends over the past year."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Scale AI Acquisition: A Game-Changer"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"In June 2025, Meta bought a majority stake in Scale AI for $14.8 billion. This gave it access to top-tier datasets, advanced testing systems, and fine-tuning capabilities. Scale’s founder, Alex Wang, now leads Meta’s AI safety and alignment efforts. The acquisition isn’t just about tools—it’s about full-stack integration, from data to deployment, giving Meta unmatched control over cost, iteration, and speed."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"LLaMA and Open-Source Advantage"}]},{"type":"image","attrs":{"src":"/imported/meta-in-2030-from-ads-to-ai-infrastructure-powerhouse/3.webp","alt":"","caption":""}},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Meta’s LLaMA models are becoming some of the most widely used open-source language models globally. While proprietary models like GPT-4o may still lead in benchmarks, LLaMA is already embedded into Meta’s own apps—Messenger, WhatsApp, Instagram—and is widely adopted by external developers."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Interestingly, Meta still uses external models like Claude for internal tools when it makes sense. This pragmatic approach puts performance over ideology."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"By open-sourcing LLaMA, Meta also builds developer trust and transparency—key advantages as regulations tighten around AI explainability."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Monetisation Without Needing New Users"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Meta continues to reach over 3 billion users monthly across its platforms. This gives it a massive edge in applying AI directly into products people already use."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"New revenue streams are appearing: Reels uses AI to improve content discovery; ad creation is being automated with generative tools; and WhatsApp/Messenger are integrating smarter business APIs and chatbots. These tools aren’t moonshots—they’re integrated into everyday use, increasing revenue per user without needing more users."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Zuckerberg’s Role in Meta’s Evolution"}]},{"type":"image","attrs":{"src":"/imported/meta-in-2030-from-ads-to-ai-infrastructure-powerhouse/4.webp","alt":"","caption":""}},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Mark Zuckerberg’s influence is still central. With control over voting shares, he can make bold long-term bets without being swayed by short-term investor pressure. While not every initiative has succeeded (e.g. the metaverse), his ability to pivot Meta ahead of industry shifts remains unmatched. The AI transition reflects this same boldness, only this time, it’s more grounded and infrastructure-led."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Data Advantage"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"AI runs on data—and Meta has more of it than almost anyone. It processes billions of interactions across text, video, voice, and images every day. These real-time, highly contextual feedback loops help train and refine its models in ways most companies can’t match. That means better personalisation, monetisation, and defensibility."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Valuing Meta’s Future, Not Its Past"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"As of June 2025, Meta trades at a forward P/E of 26x and a $1.28 trillion valuation—still largely based on its ad business legacy. But this overlooks the depth of its AI investments and growing monetisation layers."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here’s what Meta’s earnings might look like by 2030, depending on different scenarios:"}]},{"type":"table","content":[{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Scenario"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Revenue (B)"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Net Margin"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Net Income (B)"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Valuation Range (23x–35x P/E)"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Bear"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"210"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"30%"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"63"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"$1.45T – $2.21T"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Base"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"245"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"33%"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"80.85"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"$1.86T – $2.83T"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Bull"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"260"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"34%"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"88.4"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"$2.03T – $3.09T"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stretch"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"300"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"37%"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"111"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"$2.55T – $3.88T"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Even in the most conservative scenario, Meta is positioned for steady returns. The base and bull cases suggest annualised growth between 8% and 13%, driven by AI adoption, developer tools, and productivity boosts."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Final Thought: A New Meta Is Emerging"}]},{"type":"image","attrs":{"src":"/imported/meta-in-2030-from-ads-to-ai-infrastructure-powerhouse/5.webp","alt":"","caption":""}},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Meta is no longer just an ad-driven social network—it’s becoming a foundational platform for the AI era. With world-class data, full-stack infrastructure, and broad user reach, it has all the pieces to lead the next decade in tech."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Those who keep viewing Meta through the lens of its past might miss the bigger picture. The real opportunity lies in what Meta is building now, and what’s still to come."}]},{"type":"blockquote","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Written by Eeshan Karra","marks":[{"type":"italic"}]}]}]}]}'::jsonb,
    '/imported/meta-in-2030-from-ads-to-ai-infrastructure-powerhouse/1.webp',
