  (
    'is-google-stock-a-buy-in-2025',
    'Is Google Stock a Buy in 2025?',
    'Although many worry that generative AI will render search obsolete, Alphabet is busy monetising the next wave of digital infrastructure—and that creates opportunity for investors. Why Now Is an Attractive Entry Point Despite reporting one of its strongest quarters ever, Alphabet still trades like a…',
    '{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Although many worry that generative AI will render search obsolete, Alphabet is busy monetising the next wave of digital infrastructure—and that creates opportunity for investors."}]},{"type":"horizontalRule"},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Why Now Is an Attractive Entry Point"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Despite reporting one of its strongest quarters ever, Alphabet still trades like a mature ad‐only business. In reality, it’s pivoted into a foundational AI‐infrastructure player, with consumer, enterprise and physical platforms all leveraging its unparalleled data moat."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Q1 2025 Highlights","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Revenue:","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"text","text":" US $90.2 billion (↑ 12% YoY)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"EPS:","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"text","text":" US $2.81 (↑ 49% YoY)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Operating Income:","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"text","text":" US $30.6 billion (↑ 20% YoY)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Operating Margin:","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"text","text":" 34% (vs 32% in Q1 2024)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Free Cash Flow:","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"text","text":" US $19 billion"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"CapEx:","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"text","text":" US $17.2 billion"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"TTM Free Cash Flow:","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"text","text":" US $74.9 billion"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"New Quarterly Dividend:","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"text","text":" US $0.21 per share"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Alphabet has also announced a US $70 billion share buy-back. These moves reflect confidence, not desperation."}]},{"type":"horizontalRule"},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Disciplined Leadership Under Sundar Pichai"}]},{"type":"image","attrs":{"src":"/imported/is-google-stock-a-buy-in-2025/1.webp","alt":"","caption":""}},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Sundar Pichai has quietly shifted Alphabet from sprawling R&D to razor-sharp execution—without sacrificing long-term technology bets. In 2025, roughly US $75 billion of CapEx will target AI infrastructure (data centres, custom TPUs, networking), ensuring Alphabet stays ahead in model training and inference."}]},{"type":"horizontalRule"},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"AI as a Platform, Not Just a Feature"}]},{"type":"image","attrs":{"src":"/imported/is-google-stock-a-buy-in-2025/2.webp","alt":"","caption":""}},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Rather than bolt on isolated AI tools, Alphabet is weaving its Gemini models into Search, Ads, Workspace (Gmail, Docs, Meet), YouTube and Cloud:"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Search:","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"text","text":" Gemini now enhances over 100 million daily queries with richer answers and ad formats, boosting click-through rates in commercial categories."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Workspace:","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"text","text":" Contextual AI suggestions make Gmail, Docs and Meet stickier for both consumers and enterprises."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Ads:","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"text","text":" Machine-learning-driven targeting raises relevance with lower user friction."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Cloud:","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"text","text":" Vertex AI, BigQuery ML and Security AI Workbench turn Google Cloud into a profitable, AI-first rival to AWS."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This deep integration leans on Google’s multi-decade trove of indexed web data, user queries and behavioural insights—an advantage no newcomer can match."}]},{"type":"horizontalRule"},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Cloud: From Question Mark to Cash Engine"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Q1 Revenue:","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"text","text":" US $12.3 billion (↑ 28% YoY)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Profitability:","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"text","text":" Now sustainably profitable"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Major clients such as HSBC, Uber, GM, Shopify and Mayo Clinic underline that Google Cloud is critical infrastructure, not just an experiment."}]},{"type":"image","attrs":{"src":"/imported/is-google-stock-a-buy-in-2025/3.webp","alt":"","caption":""}},{"type":"horizontalRule"},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Search: Reinforced, Not Eroded"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Contrary to the bear case, search revenue hit US $50.7 billion in Q1 2025 (↑ 10% YoY) and continues to accelerate. Daily queries and mobile usage are at multi-year highs—now fuelled by AI-powered answers rather than replaced by them."}]},{"type":"horizontalRule"},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"YouTube’s Underappreciated Ecosystem"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Ad Revenue:","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"text","text":" US $8.9 billion last quarter"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Shorts Views:","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"text","text":" 70 billion+ per day"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Premium Subscribers:","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"text","text":" 100 million+"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"YouTube spans creator monetisation, TV streaming, music and live commerce. With AI-driven recommendations, rights management and ad targeting, it deserves a standalone valuation north of US $475 billion—yet still trades at a blended multiple inside Alphabet."}]},{"type":"horizontalRule"},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Waymo: A Data-Rich Physical Platform"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Waymo’s autonomous ride-hailing operates in San Francisco, Phoenix, Los Angeles and Austin—over 250,000 paid rides weekly. After raising US $5.6 billion in October 2024 (valuation ~US $45 billion), analysts forecast a US $305–850 billion valuation by 2030. Beyond cars, its real-world mapping, safety data and simulation feed back into Gemini, Maps and even in-vehicle ads."}]},{"type":"image","attrs":{"src":"/imported/is-google-stock-a-buy-in-2025/4.webp","alt":"","caption":""}},{"type":"horizontalRule"},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"A Balance Sheet Built for Offence"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Cash & Equivalents:","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"text","text":" US $95.3 billion"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Free Cash Flow (2024):","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"text","text":" US $75 billion"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Planned 2025 CapEx:","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"text","text":" US $75 billion"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This financial firepower lets Alphabet lead strategic acquisitions, scale ahead of rivals and sustain long-horizon R&D without external financing."}]},{"type":"horizontalRule"},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Antitrust: Upside in a Break-Up Scenario"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"While DOJ action looms, a forced spin-out of Search, YouTube or Cloud could unlock hidden value—each segment would likely fetch a premium valuation independently. Even without a break-up, institutional investors are increasingly modelling these businesses separately, which may re-rate the stock."}]},{"type":"image","attrs":{"src":"/imported/is-google-stock-a-buy-in-2025/5.webp","alt":"","caption":""}},{"type":"horizontalRule"},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Conclusion: A Mispriced Compounder"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"At a forward P/E of just 16.3×—well below peers like Amazon (29.5×) or Meta (23.4×)—Alphabet’s current market cap (~US $1.86 trillion) understates its AI-driven growth trajectory. Search is strengthening, Cloud is profitable, YouTube is scaling, Waymo is maturing and Gemini is everywhere. For long-term investors, the gap between perception and reality represents a rare opportunity."}]},{"type":"horizontalRule"},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This is not financial advice. Always conduct your own due diligence.","marks":[{"type":"italic"}]}]}]}'::jsonb,
    '/imported/is-google-stock-a-buy-in-2025/1.webp',
    'Is Google Stock a Buy in 2025?',
    array['AI', 'Technology']::text[],
    'Although many worry that generative AI will render search obsolete, Alphabet is busy monetising the next wave of digital infrastructure—and that creates…',
    'published',
    '2025-05-17T05:39:30.000Z'::timestamptz,
    3
  ),
  (
    'weekly-market-inspection-2-china-sxt-pharmaceuticals-inc',
    'Weekly Market Inspection #2 – China SXT Pharmaceuticals Inc',
    'Just a bit of Background: China SXT Pharmaceuticals Inc is generally considered a ‘Holding Company’ which is a term that is used to suggest that it is company that owns and subsequently has controlling interest in a another companies stock. That is, company A has a significant holding percentage…',
    '{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Just a bit of Background:"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"China SXT Pharmaceuticals Inc is generally considered a ‘Holding Company’ which is a term that is used to suggest that it is company that owns and subsequently has controlling interest in a another companies stock. That is, company A has a significant holding percentage and controlling share of company Bs stock."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The mainly focuses and engages in the research, development, manufacturing, marketing and sales of Traditional Chinese Medicines Pieces (TCMP). Some of their products include direct oral, fine and regular TCMP."}]},{"type":"image","attrs":{"src":"/imported/weekly-market-inspection-2-china-sxt-pharmaceuticals-inc/1.webp","alt":"","caption":""}},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"However, the company distributes its products under the Suxuantang Brand (SXTC), which is the primary holding company. Some of its subsidiaries include the Taizhou Su Xuan Tang Biotechnology co Ltd and also Jiangsu Su Xuan Tang Pharmecutical Co Ltd."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The company was founded by Feng Zhou in 2005 and its main quarters are located in Taizhou, China. It currently holds around 75 employees in 2024."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Some background of Feng Zhou.","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Feng Zhou has been the Chief Executive Officer and Chairman of the Board of China SXT Pharmaceuticals since July 4 2017. Previously, he has been the CEO and the vice manager of Taizhou Suxuantang. As the vice manager, he had some key responsibilities, some include his pioneering of cost formulation and effective strategization for the purchase of goods and services. Zhou graduated from Logistical Engineering University of PLA and majored in Business Administration (BA) during his time at the university."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"He is currently the companies largest stockholder."}]},{"type":"image","attrs":{"src":"/imported/weekly-market-inspection-2-china-sxt-pharmaceuticals-inc/2.webp","alt":"","caption":""}},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Feng Zhou"}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Current State"},{"type":"text","text":" – 27/4/2025"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"China SXT Pharmaceuticals Inc current stock price is 2.29 (USD) as per the American stock exchange which is a 44.49% increase since its last update. The company has a volume of 38.04 million which as emphasized by a 2.19 million relative volume which is above its average volume of 17.36 million, suggests there has been more activity of the buying and selling of shares than usual. The company also has a market cap of 38.52 million USD which means that the SXTC is currently running on a micro-cap, suggesting lower stability for investors and shareholders, increased volatility, but a greater current return."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The companies P/E ratio is currently at 0.84 which insinuates there is a potential over-valuation but rather a positive trajectory on future growth. This is a calculated metric which takes into account the diluted EPS (earnings per share) which is currently sitting at a 2.73 USD, which implies that the company is currently profitable and will continue to be that way."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"One thing to mention is that although there has been a positive outlook on the companies current and future position, SXTC still has a micro-cap which means that there is going to be expected short term down-turns, emphasizing the risk and volatility associated with such an acquisition."}]},{"type":"image","attrs":{"src":"/imported/weekly-market-inspection-2-china-sxt-pharmaceuticals-inc/3.webp","alt":"","caption":""}},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Just a note on the Pharmaceutical market, my personal view is that the Pharmaceutical market in its entirety is an extremely risky stock option for investors, this is due to the sole fact that there is so much testing, regulation compliance and standards that need to be met."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Not to mention, one negative result can deter the procedural confidence of a company which means that although there may be positive signs based on media-frenzy for a potential medicinal drug to exist based on current trial tests, it can always spiral and sway public confidence if the medicinal drugs or are not successfully passed through."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Outlook on Valuation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"China SXT Pharmaceuticals has seen an astounding increase in the market-cap performance, seeing it has increased by 4025.70% in the past 12 months. The company’s P/S ratio (a financial metric that is used to suggest that how much investors are willing to pay for each dollar of a company’s revenue) is 2.81, which may suggest that there is an overvalued but expecting a very high expected growth rate towards to the near future. One thing to note is that the market capitalization has increased tremendously, therefore, its change may have outweighed the companies revenue growth, which using income statement statics, amounts to +6.78% TTM YoY (Trailing 12 months, Year on Year)."}]},{"type":"image","attrs":{"src":"/imported/weekly-market-inspection-2-china-sxt-pharmaceuticals-inc/4.webp","alt":"","caption":""}},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The P/C ratio is currently sitting at 0.40, which suggests that the stock is not too undervalued by investors based on the cash at hand as per the balance sheet (18.51 M USD), potentially signifying that investors are optimistic about positive cash on hand returns within the future."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Just a reminder that sales revenue doesn’t exactly equal the amount of cash that is on hand."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Why did this Occur?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The company had regained compliance with the Nasdaq Listing Rule 5550(a)(2) and has fulfilled the minimum bid price in order to enter the market, therefore giving a reason to explain why there was such a drastic increase in the stock price, as well as seeing improvements in things like volatility, liquidity and capital inflow."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The company had received a notification letter from Nasdaq on October 3rd 2024, there was an indication of a failure to meet the minimum big rice of US$1.00 for 30 consecutive business days under the Minimum Bid Price Requirement."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Just to elaborate further, listing a company such as China SXT Pharmaceuticals on a very tech driven stock exchange such as Nasdaq can open the company up to more investors. This leads to an enhancement of economic growth due to an increased rate of company expansion through higher capital inflows."}]},{"type":"image","attrs":{"src":"/imported/weekly-market-inspection-2-china-sxt-pharmaceuticals-inc/5.webp","alt":"","caption":""}},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Key Takeaways:"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Although volatile, there is a positive projection for future growth"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Investors are assuming there are higher cash on hand returns due to an increase in market capitalization"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Increased Stock Price due to Nasdaq listing"}]}]}]}]}'::jsonb,
