  (
    'weekly-market-inspection-1-aspire-mining-ltd',
    'Weekly Market Inspection #1 – ASPIRE MINING LTD',
    'Just a bit of background, Aspire Mining Ltd is a mining exploration and development company, the company undergoes key processes including the acquisition, exploration and development of minerals properties. The company operates around the world including Australia, Mongolia and Singapore. The…',
    '{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Just a bit of background,"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Aspire Mining Ltd is a mining exploration and development company, the company undergoes key processes including the acquisition, exploration and development of minerals properties. The company operates around the world including Australia, Mongolia and Singapore."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The company was founded on October 30, 2006 in Sydney, Australia, however, it was not established purely from one individual. Rather, the current Chairman of Aspire Ltd Micheal (Mick) Avery, had led the evolvement of a team of individuals that development of the Baarun Noyon Uul coal mine in Mongolia."}]},{"type":"image","attrs":{"src":"/imported/weekly-market-inspection-1-aspire-mining-ltd/1.webp","alt":"","caption":""}},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Today, Aspire Mining Ltd is a public company that generates much of its income and revenues from the Coal Mining Sector. According to IBIS, information of the number of employees within the firm is not available but in 2023, the company generated $593,000 including sales and other revenues."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"What’s currently going on?"},{"type":"text","text":" 17th April"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"As of 10:58pm, 17th of April 2025, Aspire Limited is at a stock price of 0.230 AUD which is which is -0.030 from its last update at 2:18pm, this consequentially led to a -11.54% fall in its share price."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The companies current volume is sitting at 499.66K with a relative volume of 3.96, this suggests that the average volume of shares that are exchanged in the market for Aspire Ltd stock is 126.17K. Considering that there has been a considerable fall in the stock price (-11.54%), there has been growing momentum for investors to sell their shares as a result, enhancing the it’s volatility."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Its market-cap is in fact 131.19M, a micro-cap which although volatile, may actually exhibit future growth potential for investors which is backed by it P/E ratio of 11.73, which currently insinuates that the company is overvalued."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, there are two contradicting perspectives, we have one side that says that there has been a considerable fall of the stock price down to 0.230 AUD, but the the P/E ratio and market-cap may suggest future growth. What I do what want to shift our attention onto is the EPS dilution, which is essentially the amount of profits which a company is earning for each outstanding share of common stock. The EPS takes into account any outstanding stocks which means that it is much broader and useful for investors to make their assumptions."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The EPS dilution for Aspire Mining Ltd is 0.02 AUD, which actually means that the positive metric highlights that the company is still making a profit but it’s at a point that is not as prominent as before."}]},{"type":"image","attrs":{"src":"/imported/weekly-market-inspection-1-aspire-mining-ltd/2.webp","alt":"","caption":""}},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Why might this be the case though, what might have caused this dramatic downward trajectory?","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Aspire Mining Ltd has completed surveys at the Erdenet Rail Terminal Site in Mongolia, which is a key area for the Ovoot Coking Coal Project. The terminal"},{"type":"text","text":" “will facilitate efficient coal transloading, enhance operational efficiency, and create over 100 local jobs, aligning with Aspire’s goal of becoming a leading supplier of premium Mongolian coking coal.","marks":[{"type":"italic"}]},{"type":"text","text":"” according to the Microsoft Network (MSN)."}]},{"type":"image","attrs":{"src":"/imported/weekly-market-inspection-1-aspire-mining-ltd/3.webp","alt":"","caption":""}},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Then again, this should technically affect the the company’s stocks positively right due to increased productional efficiency; but it has been reported by "},{"type":"text","text":"Simply Wall Street","marks":[{"type":"italic"}]},{"type":"text","text":" that there has been a cash-burn within the company, meaning that the company isn’t generating as much revenue and using its available cash to fund and expand operations. "},{"type":"text","text":"“Since it has a market capitalization of US$71m, Aspire Mining’s US$2.9m in cash burn equates to about 4.1% of its market value.","marks":[{"type":"italic"}]},{"type":"text","text":"” (2024)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This is a relatively low percentage for a cash-burn in comparison to the grand scheme, which means that investors can be covered by obtaining company loans according to "},{"type":"text","text":"Simply Wall Street. ","marks":[{"type":"italic"}]},{"type":"text","text":"However, a problem arises with trying to reduce the cash-burn, leading to a fall in liquidity, which may have negatively affected investor and shareholder confidence, therefore allowing them to sell their stocks – causing the price to fall."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Overall Picture – Short and Sharp"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Overevaluation and positive outlook for future growth based on current metrics"}]}]}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Increased developments for the Erdenet Rail Terminal Site in Mongolia"}]}]}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Investors may have sold their current stocks due to inability to reduce cash-burns"}]}]}]}]}'::jsonb,
    '/imported/weekly-market-inspection-1-aspire-mining-ltd/1.webp',
    'Weekly Market Inspection #1 – ASPIRE MINING LTD',
    array['Business', 'Stock Market']::text[],
    'Just a bit of background, Aspire Mining Ltd is a mining exploration and development company, the company undergoes key processes including the acquisition…',
