    '2025-04-19T05:37:21.000Z'::timestamptz,
    3
  ),
  (
    'careers-in-finance-which-path-should-you-pick',
    'Careers in Finance – Which Path Should You Pick?',
    'Finance… an industry often misinterpreted as an environment filled with number crunching, long hours, anonymity and ambiguity is always filled with a motivation. The general population just don’t know it. Each position, sub-field and hierarchy always has an end goal that needs to be achieved. Yes…',
    '{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Finance… an industry often misinterpreted as an environment filled with number crunching, long hours, anonymity and ambiguity is always filled with a motivation. The general population just don’t know it. Each position, sub-field and hierarchy always has an end goal that needs to be achieved. Yes, it can be tedious to achieve those ambitions, but when an specialist in the industry does their required task, there is always passion behind it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Some may say that the industry is becoming too saturated, others may say that there is sub-optimal pay for their standards, others may even suggest that the industry as a whole is too complex to understand due to its intricacies. Take the coveted Wall Street for example, not only is it extremely difficult and off-putting to overcome its barrier and enter its gates, but the charts, boards, rush and adrenaline that lies behind its buildings gives the general onlooker a chill, an environment that is too hot to handle."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"For those behind the walls, the stock brokers, the analysts, the financial analysts, the investment bankers and the private equity analysts, there is always a common theme, that an ever changing society which is advancing into a new technological age is always building new businesses and cooperation’s that need their skills and expertise in some for or another."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Take DeepSeek for example. A cheap and reliable AI Chatbot released to the public in early 2025, it has almost revolutionized not only the engineering sector but also the financial forecasting and modelling sector according to Medium."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"So what are solid careers in Finance in a new and evolving society? Lets take a quick look at the 4 below.","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"image","attrs":{"src":"/imported/careers-in-finance-which-path-should-you-pick/2.webp","alt":"","caption":""}},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"1. Financial Analyst"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Primarily responsible in analyzing financial data, they also guide businesses and individuals in order to maximize future profits (US Bureau of Labor Statistics) . They also play critical roles in things like risk and investment management and strategy recommendations in order to improve financial circumstance."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Although quite tedious, it is reccomended that after considerable hours, a CFA (Chartered Financial Analyst) certification should be attained, as it is a key metric that can advance individuals in the field."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Salary (Glassdoor , Melbourne 2025) : $90,000","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"2. Investment Banking Analyst"}]},{"type":"image","attrs":{"src":"/imported/careers-in-finance-which-path-should-you-pick/3.webp","alt":"","caption":""}},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Investment Bankers… time, time and more time!!! I mean that is what the general population assume, which is true, there are a lot of hours that need to be considered when pursuing a career within this sub-field."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"On a more general note, Investment Bankers work with different company’s in order to obtain sales targets, advise companies on potential targets and recommend terms according to the CFI. Although IB is much more than this, it is a very lucrative career which is high in demand not only now but for the future due to the ever-changing landscape of the business world. More and more businesses and companies are being made to adapt to a technological revolution, which means that in turn, more Investment Bankers in order to help shape economies and corporate landscapes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Although fierce in competition it is great for an entry-level position. Then again, it does help with some prior experience, it is a highly coveted position in the finance industry."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Salary (Seek, Melbourne 2025) : $110,000 – $130,000","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"3. Financial Advsior"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Financial Advisors essentially assess the needs of the individual about their business and help them with their investment decisions, knowledge on tax laws and insurance (US Bureau of Labor Statistics)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"What is important to understand with this, is that I believe that as topics like software engineering and artificial intelligence becomes more and more popular – as seen with the emergence of AI chatbots like ChatGPT and DeepSeek AI, more and more individuals who would want to start small business will want to integrate these systems. This is especially of concern as more individuals, within Australia and overseas are keen to study undergraduate degrees like Computer Science."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Hence, Financial Advisors within, lets just say 2030-2040, will be necessary as in order to advise individuals about the impact of investing in such large and controversial AI Bots to help enhance their business and computational systems."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Salary (Glassdoor, Melbourne 2025): $110,000-$130,000","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"4. Trading Analyst"}]},{"type":"image","attrs":{"src":"/imported/careers-in-finance-which-path-should-you-pick/4.webp","alt":"","caption":""}},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Trading Analysts on the other hand assess Financial Markets and seek possible trading opportunities to maximize profits for businesses."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Although it may seem simple, it is quite the opposite."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You see, trading can be complex, buying and selling assets, stocks, assessing currencies, so what is recommended is that you take your time to learn the art of Investing as a foundation. It is at this position that you can take another 6 months to learn the more holistic approach when it comes to trading as it is very intricate in its details (The Freedom Trader)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"To make the best possible career in trading, it can start from even an early age! In todays society, there are courses online that can be used to learn the craft which can instill skills and disciplines which be used for future use."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now lets redirect ourselves, why is trading a solid career for the future? Lets take Trump for example. No-one, not even current Australian Prime Minister Anthony Albanese expected such a move , not at the time, but even long before! His policies and initiatives changed markets dearly, making it harder for businesses to cope, as reflected in the ASX 200 in the past week. This meant that traders had to look at price distortions based on these long term supply changes which was dramatic in itself."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Not to mention. The market itself is changing day to day regardless. So traders will in fact be in demand. Especially as new and evolving technologies take over the landscape."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Salary (Glassdoor, Melbourne 2025) : $80,000 – $100,000","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"blockquote","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"“Financial freedom is available for those who learn about it and work for it”"}]}]}]}'::jsonb,
    '/imported/careers-in-finance-which-path-should-you-pick/1.webp',
    'Careers in Finance – Which Path Should You Pick?',
    array['Personal Finance']::text[],
    'Finance… an industry often misinterpreted as an environment filled with number crunching, long hours, anonymity and ambiguity is always filled with a…',
    'published',
    '2025-04-12T10:15:44.000Z'::timestamptz,
    4
  ),
  (
    'best-stock-analysis-tools-for-2025',
    'Best Stock Analysis Tools for 2025',
    'Investing in stocks can feel daunting with an overload of data, making it tough to figure out what really counts. That’s why stock analysis tools are essential—they provide the insights you need to make more informed decisions. As we step into 2025, I’ve compiled a list of the top stock analysis…',
    '{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Investing in stocks can feel daunting with an overload of data, making it tough to figure out what really counts. That’s why stock analysis tools are essential—they provide the insights you need to make more informed decisions. As we step into 2025, I’ve compiled a list of the top stock analysis tools designed to help you navigate the clutter. We’ll explore each tool’s advantages and drawbacks, and I’ll wrap up with my personal favourite. Let’s get started!"}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Key Attributes of an Outstanding Stock Analysis Tool"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Before diving into the lineup, here’s what I considered:"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"• Data Accuracy – Reliable information is essential."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"• Robust Features – The more functionalities available, the better."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"• User-Friendly Interface – A simple, intuitive design saves time."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"• Cost Efficiency – Free or affordable options are a plus."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Every tool has its unique advantages, so let’s explore how they stack up."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"#1 GuruFocus"}]},{"type":"image","attrs":{"src":"/imported/best-stock-analysis-tools-for-2025/1.webp","alt":"","caption":""}},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A Data-Heavy Powerhouse","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"If you love delving into details, GuruFocus is tailored for you. This platform brims with diverse valuation methods, including discounted cash flow (DCF), P/E ratios, and price-to-book metrics. It also supplies a wealth of historical data and fosters an active community for idea sharing. However, take note that some of its premium features are accessible only through costly subscriptions, and the interface might be a bit complex for beginners. Still, for the avid, detail-oriented investor, it’s a veritable treasure trove."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Pros:","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"• Comprehensive valuation tools"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"• Moat rating"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"• Extensive historical data"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"• Active community"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Cons:","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"• Premium features come at an extra cost"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"• Not particularly beginner-friendly"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"• Subscriptions range from $500 to $2400 per year"}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"#2 PEvaluator"}]},{"type":"image","attrs":{"src":"/imported/best-stock-analysis-tools-for-2025/2.webp","alt":"","caption":""}},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Take Command of Your Analysis","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Looking for a tool that puts you in the driver’s seat? PEvaluator lets you build custom market models tailored to your investment approach, delivering fair price estimates on thousands of stocks. It offers features such as P/E analysis, moat ratings, comprehensive stock comparisons, portfolio tracking, and price alerts—all designed to empower smarter, more efficient investing."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Pros:","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"• Intuitive interface"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"• Customisable market models with intrinsic value estimates"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"• Wide array of analytical tools"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"• Extensive historical financial data—all for just $10/month"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Cons:","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"• The free tier is restricted to mega-cap stocks only"}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"#3 Finchat"}]},{"type":"image","attrs":{"src":"/imported/best-stock-analysis-tools-for-2025/3.webp","alt":"","caption":""}},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Your Conversational Stock Assistant","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Imagine having an AI companion to break down stocks for you—that’s FinChat. This tool blends intelligent, AI-driven insights with robust financial data, enabling you to screen stocks based on over 300 metrics or simply ask questions like you would to a financial expert. It’s designed with ease-of-use in mind and even offers a free tier for starters. If you appreciate tech-forward solutions and desire rapid, interactive answers, FinChat could be an excellent choice."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Pros:","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"• AI-powered insights"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"• User-friendly interface"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"• Free tier available"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"• Access to a global stock database"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Cons:","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"• Relatively new and less established"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"• May not offer the depth of analysis found in some legacy tools"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"• AI-generated responses require verification"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"• Optimal use requires an upgrade to the $80/month tier"}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"#4 Simply Wallstreet"}]},{"type":"image","attrs":{"src":"/imported/best-stock-analysis-tools-for-2025/4.webp","alt":"","caption":""}},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Visually Appealing Choice","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"If you’re new to investing, Simply Wall St might be right up your alley. It simplifies intricate valuation reports into clear, readable insights using a straightforward DCF model, and its free basic features are perfect for beginners. Plus, with a mobile app to monitor stocks on the go, it keeps you connected wherever you are. However, customisation is quite limited, and sometimes the data isn’t as up-to-date as you’d like. Overall, it’s an excellent option if you value simplicity and clarity over extensive detail."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Pros:","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"• Easy-to-understand reports"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"• Free basic features"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"• Clean, intuitive design"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"• Affordable at $20/month"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Cons:","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"• Limited customisation options"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"• Occasional data lag"}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"#5 Koyfin"}]},{"type":"image","attrs":{"src":"/imported/best-stock-analysis-tools-for-2025/5.webp","alt":"","caption":""}},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A Graph-Heavy Power Tool for Investors","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Koyfin operates like a Swiss Army knife for those who crave data. It offers advanced charting, fully customizable dashboards, and a screener featuring over 500 metrics—including both fundamental and technical indicators. The free version is impressively robust, and you can even download your analyses for further exploration. On the flip side, it has a learning curve, and serious users might find the free plan a bit limiting. It’s a great choice for data enthusiasts who don’t mind a bit of initial setup. Popular among day traders who do more chart analysis work as well."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Pros:","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"• Extensive metrics"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"• High-quality charts"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"• Generous free tier"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"• Ability to download data"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Cons:","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"• Requires time to master"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"• Performance can be sluggish at times"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"• Interface might feel cluttered"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"• Subscription plans range from $50 to $200 per month"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Choosing the best stock analysis tool really depends on your specific needs. If you love diving deep into the details, GuruFocus is ideal. For a more straightforward experience, Simply Wall St delivers clarity, while FinChat offers a modern twist with its AI-powered insights. Koyfin, on the other hand, is perfect for those who thrive on rich, data-driven visuals. However, if you’re looking for a tool that adapts to your personal investing style, PEvaluator stands out as my top pick. Give it a try and share your feedback—happy investing!"}]}]}'::jsonb,
    '/imported/best-stock-analysis-tools-for-2025/1.webp',
