    1
  ),
  (
    'journey-into-the-stock-market',
    'Journey into the stock market',
    'The magic that emerges from effective collaboration is undeniable. When diverse minds converge with a shared purpose, the results can be transformative.',
    '{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Investing always felt intimidating to me. Stocks, ETFs, mutual funds—it sounded like a language I didn’t understand. But once I took my first step, I realised it’s simpler than it seems."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Make sure that before anything you learn about how investing works. Whether it be bonds, stocks, crypto, or even options, having a comprehensive understanding is crucial."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Investing without knowledge is worse than gambling."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Why I Started Investing"}]},{"type":"image","attrs":{"src":"/imported/journey-into-the-stock-market/1.webp","alt":"","caption":""}},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wanted my money to grow rather than sit idle in a savings account. Investing allows your money to work for you, thanks to the power of compound interest. The earlier you start, the more time your investments have to grow."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"How I Got Started"}]},{"type":"orderedList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Research","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"text","text":": I began by learning the basics—what stocks, bonds, and ETFs are—through free resources like Investopedia and YouTube channels. In the useful links section there will be some great resources."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Choose a Platform","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"text","text":": I opened an account on a beginner-friendly platform that offers low fees and easy access to investments. For the Australian consumer, I found Spaceship good for their managed funds, yet bad for their diversity and transaction speed. Etoro is good for their diversity, copy trading, low transaction fees but has high currency exchange rates."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Start Small","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"text","text":": My first investment was in an index fund (Vanguard S&P 500 growth ETF), which spreads risk across a variety of companies. Starting with small amounts helped me build confidence."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"▶ Watch the video on YouTube","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8Ij7A1VCB7I"}}]}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Key Lesson"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Investing isn’t about timing the market—it’s about time "},{"type":"text","text":"in","marks":[{"type":"italic"}]},{"type":"text","text":" the market. Consistent contributions, even small ones, can grow significantly over time. If I can do it, so can you."}]}]}'::jsonb,
    '/imported/journey-into-the-stock-market/2.webp',
