  (
    'budgeting-for-beginners',
    'Budgeting for Beginners',
    'What fosters effective teamwork? It’s not just about grouping individuals together and hoping for the best. It’s about cultivating an environment where trust, open communication, mutual respect, and a shared vision converge.',
    '{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Budgeting used to feel restrictive to me, but now I see it as freedom—freedom to save, invest, and spend on what truly matters. Here’s how I started budgeting and how you can, too:"}]},{"type":"image","attrs":{"src":"/imported/budgeting-for-beginners/1.webp","alt":"","caption":""}},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Why Budgeting Matters"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A budget isn’t about saying “no” to everything fun; it’s about having a plan for your money. It ensures you’re in control, rather than wondering where your money went at the end of the month."}]},{"type":"blockquote","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"“A budget is telling your money where to go instead of wondering where it went.”","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"– Dave Ramsey"}]}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"My Simple Budgeting Process"}]},{"type":"orderedList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Track Your Spending","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"text","text":": For one month, I tracked every dollar I spent to understand where my money was going. This helped me identify unnecessary expenses."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Set Categories","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"text","text":": I divided my spending into categories like rent, groceries, entertainment, and savings. Then I assigned a realistic amount to each category based on my income."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Use Tools","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"text","text":": I use a budgeting app to keep things organized. Apps like Mint and YNAB make it easy to track spending and adjust as needed excpecially for people with diverse expenses. However for the common man, a spreadsheet like this is perfect: "},{"type":"text","text":"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1qC11pdB_S7ZZZxevoHut_JjdlH28BA__wAzg-SroSj4/edit?usp=sharing","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1qC11pdB_S7ZZZxevoHut_JjdlH28BA__wAzg-SroSj4/edit?usp=sharing"}}]}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"▶ Watch the video on YouTube","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WhULO7JJB9o"}}]}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Staying on Track"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The key to sticking with a budget is flexibility. Life happens, and some months you’ll overspend. What matters is getting back on track and staying committed to your goals."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Budgeting is a skill anyone can learn, and it’s the foundation of financial success. Start today and take the first step toward financial freedom."}]}]}'::jsonb,
    '/imported/budgeting-for-beginners/2.webp',
    'Budgeting for Beginners',
    array['Personal Finance', 'Beginners']::text[],
    'What fosters effective teamwork? It’s not just about grouping individuals together and hoping for the best. It’s about cultivating an environment where trust…',
    'published',
